---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Doodle from '../components/Doodle.astro';
import Hamster from '../components/Hamster.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base side="both" title="Colophon" description="How this site is built, and what it is set in.">
  <h1 class="text-[2rem] font-bold tracking-tight">
    <span class="relative inline-block">
      Colophon
      <Doodle kind="underline" class="absolute -bottom-1.5 left-0 w-full h-2.5 text-accent/70" />
    </span>
  </h1>

  <p class="mt-4 text-ink-2 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
    Every book used to end with a note about how it was made. This is that note.
  </p>

  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="label">Set in</h2>
    <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4">
      <div>
        <dt class="font-medium text-ink font-display text-[1.15rem]">Bricolage Grotesque</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] text-ink-2 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">
          Headings. A variable grotesque whose narrow weights are frankly a bit anxious, which felt right.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="font-medium text-ink text-[1.15rem]">Fraunces</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] text-ink-2 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">
          Body text, with its <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">SOFT</code> and
          <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">WONK</code> axes turned away from their sensible defaults. That is where the
          slightly wobbly serifs come from.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="font-medium text-ink font-tc text-[1.2rem]">LXGW WenKai TC 霞鶩文楷</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] text-ink-2 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">
          All Chinese text, including every poem. A kai face derived from Fontworks&rsquo; Klee One — it looks written
          rather than set, which matters more on this site than anywhere else.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="font-medium text-ink aside-hand text-[1.4rem]">Caveat</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] text-ink-2 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">The margin scrawls, in biro blue.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="font-medium text-ink font-mono text-[1rem]">JetBrains Mono</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] text-ink-2 mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">Dates, code, and the small capital labels.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="label">Built with</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
      Astro, with React only for the one canvas animation on the physics page. Tailwind plus a hand-written stylesheet.
      Math by KaTeX. Traditional-to-Simplified conversion by OpenCC, in the browser, so the poems ship once and convert
      on demand.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
      The ruled paper, the red margin line and the wobbly boxes are all CSS — gradients and an abused
      <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em]">border-radius</code>. The doodles are inline SVG paths with deliberately
      misaligned control points. No illustration files, nothing to load.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
      It builds to static files and is copied to a small VPS over SSH by a shell script, where Caddy serves it. There is
      no CI, no platform, and no database. Source is on <a href={site.github} class="text-accent">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="label">The seal</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-ink-2 leading-relaxed flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
      <span class="seal" aria-hidden="true">連宏勛</span>
      <span
        >The red block beside the poems is a name seal, <span class="font-tc">印章</span>. Printed collections carry one
        in vermilion seal paste; here it is just a border and a colour, which is cheating, but the colour is right.</span
      >
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="label">What this site does not do</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-ink-2">
      {
        [
          'No analytics. I do not know you are here.',
          'No cookies, so no cookie banner.',
          'No newsletter modal, no “subscribe to keep reading”.',
          'No fonts or scripts beyond the two font CDNs listed above.',
          'No AI-generated text or images anywhere in the poems, the physics, or the prose.',
        ].map((line) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-accent/60 shrink-0 select-none font-mono text-[0.9rem] pt-0.5">▸</span>
            <span>{line}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="label">Take the button</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <img
        src="/buttons/hhungxun.svg"
        alt="Heah Hung Xun · 連宏勛 — 88 by 31 web button"
        class="button88"
        width="88"
        height="31"
      />
      <code class="text-[0.75rem] text-muted font-mono">88 × 31, as is traditional</code>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[0.92rem] text-ink-2">
      Hotlinking is fine, but a copy on your own server is kinder to both of us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="mt-14 flex items-end gap-3">
    <span class="text-accent/60 shrink-0 wiggle-hover"><Hamster size={52} /></span>
    <span class="aside-hand pb-1">↑↑↓↓←→←→BA, if you are curious.</span>
  </p>
</Base>
